# cs-website — THIS REPOSITORY PUBLISHES.
#
# docs/ is served at https://simplexvia.com. More importantly, anything ever
# committed stays readable in git history even after a later commit deletes it.
# A file removed next week is still public. So the rule is not "clean it up
# later" — it is "never let it in".
#
# The source of truth is ai-business/website/. docs/ is an rsync mirror of it
# (deploy_website.sh). Nothing in docs/ is edited by hand.
#
# To publish something these rules block, override deliberately and knowingly:
#     git add -f <file>

# ---- Internal business material ---------------------------------------------
# These follow the naming convention used in ai-business/. If one is ever copied
# here by accident, git refuses it rather than quietly publishing the rate card.
*_INTERNAL.*
Pricing_*
Negotiation_*
Scoping_*
*_Prompt.md
CLAUDE.md

# ---- Client material ---------------------------------------------------------
clients/
client_results/
*_Audit.*
*_Action_Plan*
*HANDOVER*
*HANDOFF*

# ---- Working formats ---------------------------------------------------------
# Spreadsheets, decks and documents are internal here without exception.
# A genuine public download is the rare case — use git add -f for it.
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.docx
*.doc
*.pptx
*.ppt
*.pdf
*.csv

# ---- Credentials -------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*_token*
*secret*
credentials*

# ---- Jekyll build output -----------------------------------------------------
# docs/.nojekyll turns the build off, but these appear if it is ever run locally.
_site/
.jekyll-cache/
.jekyll-metadata
Gemfile.lock
vendor/
node_modules/

# ---- OS and editor junk ------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
